devil's first six  issues before he switched to all red  gow told collider that many characters  were unavailable for inclusion in  she-hulk due to conflicts with other mcu  properties at first she assumed that the  same was true of daredevil but the  writing team soon found out otherwise  gow said we thought we were being  pranked we just kept writing him in and  we kept rolling with the story just  thinking like okay any moment now  they're going to tell us we can't use  them they made a mistake they actually  don't have the rights but it just kept  becoming more and more real in july of  2022 marvel studios revealed that it's  in the process of working on a new  daredevil series titled daredevil born  again it's entirely possible that his  appearance in she-hulk will serve as a  prelude to his upcoming starring vehicle  could the fact that his suit is now  somewhat different in appearance suggest  we're dealing with a different devil  than the one who exclaimed in 2018 i  beat you or is this merely a new chapter  for an established character we'll leave  jen to find that out as she-hulk  continues
 

